  "contract": "offline-tokens/v2 Tier C binding, replayed through the tier-c-approval/v1 admission",
  "note": "Replayed with the admission model of tier-c-approval/vectors/admission.json, whose note defines every event and expectation, against the `proposal` below. `token` holds the payload claims after decoding; signature verification precedes every rule here and is replayed by signing-domain.json, not here. `consumed_token_ids` lists the `token_id` values a durable approval already claimed. `token_consumed` is whether the step's `token_id` is claimed. `token_format` is how the payload parses: `v1` without a `token_version` claim, `v2` when it is the JSON integer 2, and `malformed` otherwise, including a Boolean, a string or `2.0`. `expires_at` and `issued_at` are unix seconds, as the contract states. `host_state_token_cases` present an offline token for a host-state Tier C action on the existing approval workflow, outside tier-c-approval/v1: `expected` is `refused` for a token of either version, because no v1 token approves any Tier C action and a host-state Tier C action has no commissioned zone for a v2 token to bind, and `token_consumed` is whether its `token_id` is claimed.",
